IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `itaa-cgt`

-- Income Tax Assessment Act 1997 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- capital gains amounts the text deposit could not compute, now
-- computed from the formulas the Federal Register prints as images: the partial main residence exemption (s 118-185), and
-- the discount percentage of an individual who was a foreign or temporary resident for part of the time (ss 115-100(c),
-- 115-105, 115-115(2), (3)).
--
-- A module beside itaa-cgt.l4 (24 October 2026). itaa-cgt.l4 answers only a home that was the main residence throughout
-- (ss 118-110, 118-150), and takes the individual to be neither a foreign nor a temporary resident; it lists ss 118-185 and
-- 115-105 to 115-120 as not encoded. It stays as it is; this module calls its `What is my net capital gain` rather than
-- restating it.
--
-- SEAT: the taxpayer -- an individual who sells a home they lived in for part of the time, or an asset held while they were a
-- foreign or temporary resident for part of the time ("What capital gain do I make?").
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 267 (register id C2026C00400), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A05138.txt. The
-- formulas are transcribed in ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A05138.formulas.md (entries s 118-185(2), s 115-115(2),
-- (3)(b); recovered 2026-10-24), and encoded from there.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. The absence rule (s 118-145) and the other choices that let a dwelling count as the main residence for days it
-- was not lived in: the person states the non-main residence days after any choice made; use for producing income
-- (s 118-190, a "reasonable" amount); s 118-192 (first used to produce income after 20 August 1996); deceased estates
-- (ss 118-195 to 118-200); s 115-115(4) to (6) (a discount testing period starting on or before 8 May 2012 for someone who was
-- then a foreign or temporary resident: answered `not covered`); the residency changes of s 115-105(3) (the person states the
-- days as that subsection treats them); trusts (ss 115-110, 115-120).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the individual's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No
-- pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Income Tax Assessment Act 1997 -- capital gains amounts from the formulas`

§§ `118-185 -- partial exemption for a home that was my main residence for part of the time`

-- s 118-185(1): "You get only a partial exemption for a *CGT event that happens in relation to a *dwelling or your *ownership
-- interest in it if: (a) you are an individual; and (b) the dwelling was your main residence for part only of your *ownership
-- period; and (c) the interest did not *pass to you as a beneficiary in, and you did not *acquire it as a trustee of, the estate
-- of a deceased person." (3): not if you "(a) are an *excluded foreign resident; or (b) are a foreign resident who does not
-- satisfy the *life events test".
-- (2), from the authorised rendering:   CG or CL amount × (Non-main residence days / Days in your *ownership period)
-- "CG or CL amount is the *capital gain or *capital loss you would have made from the *CGT event apart from this Subdivision.
-- non-main residence days is the number of days in your *ownership period when the *dwelling was not your main residence."
DECLARE `Partial exemption` IS ONE OF
    `capital gain or loss` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `not covered: s 118-185 does not apply (not an individual, inherited or held as trustee, or an excluded foreign resident)`
    `not covered: the dwelling was the main residence throughout, or never (see itaa-cgt.l4)`

@export What capital gain or loss do I make on a home that was my main residence for only part of the time I owned it (s 118-185)?
GIVEN `gain or loss apart from the main residence rules` IS A NUMBER @desc The capital gain you would make apart from Subdivision 118-B, in dollars (a capital loss as a negative number)
      `non-main residence days` IS A NUMBER @desc The days in your ownership period when the dwelling was not your main residence (after any choice under s 118-145 or s 118-150)
      `days in my ownership period` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days in your ownership period
      `an individual, not through a deceased estate, and not an excluded foreign resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an individual who did not inherit the dwelling or hold it as trustee of an estate, and are not an excluded foreign resident or a foreign resident failing the life events test
GIVETH A `Partial exemption`
`What gain do I make on a home that was my main residence for part of the time` MEANS
    IF NOT `an individual, not through a deceased estate, and not an excluded foreign resident`
    THEN `not covered: s 118-185 does not apply (not an individual, inherited or held as trustee, or an excluded foreign resident)`
    ELSE IF `non-main residence days` AT MOST 0 OR `non-main residence days` AT LEAST `days in my ownership period`
         THEN `not covered: the dwelling was the main residence throughout, or never (see itaa-cgt.l4)`
         ELSE `capital gain or loss` ((`gain or loss apart from the main residence rules` TIMES `non-main residence days`) DIVIDED BY `days in my ownership period`)

§§ `115-100(c), 115-105, 115-115 -- the discount percentage of a foreign or temporary resident for part of the time`

-- s 115-105(2): applies to an individual's *discount capital gain if the discount testing period ("starting on the day you
-- acquired the CGT asset; and ... ending on the day the CGT event happens") ends after 8 May 2012 and "(e) you were a foreign
-- resident or *temporary resident during some or all of so much of that period as is after 8 May 2012."
-- s 115-100(c): the discount percentage is then "the percentage resulting from section 115-115". The paragraph has no date
-- limit: unlike (aa), it still applies to a gain from a CGT event on or after 1 July 2027.
-- s 115-115(2), "If the discount testing period starts after 8 May 2012", from the authorised rendering:
--     Number of days during discount testing period that you were an Australian resident (but not a *temporary resident)
--         / (2 × Number of days in discount testing period)
-- (3), if it starts on or before 8 May 2012 and "you were an Australian resident (but not a *temporary resident) on 8 May 2012":
--     (Number of days in discount testing period − Number of apportionable days that you were a foreign resident or *temporary
--      resident) / (2 × Number of days in discount testing period)
-- "apportionable day means a day, after 8 May 2012, during the discount testing period." Both are "expressed as a percentage";
-- no rounding is given.
DECLARE `Foreign resident discount` IS ONE OF
    `discount percentage` HAS `percent` IS A NUMBER
    `not covered: the period starts on or before 8 May 2012 and you were then a foreign or temporary resident (s 115-115(4) to (6))`

@export What is my CGT discount percentage if I was a foreign or temporary resident for part of the time I held the asset (s 115-115(2), (3))?
GIVEN `discount testing period starts after 8 May 2012` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you acquired the asset after 8 May 2012
      `resident and not temporary on 8 May 2012` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were an Australian resident, and not a temporary resident, on 8 May 2012 (asked only if you acquired the asset on or before that day)
      `days in the discount testing period` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days from the day you acquired the asset to the day of the CGT event
      `days I was an Australian resident and not a temporary resident` IS A NUMBER @desc The days in that period you were an Australian resident and not a temporary resident (used if you acquired the asset after 8 May 2012)
      `days after 8 May 2012 I was a foreign or temporary resident` IS A NUMBER @desc The days in that period, after 8 May 2012, you were a foreign or temporary resident (used if you acquired it on or before 8 May 2012)
GIVETH A `Foreign resident discount`
`What is my discount percentage as a part-time foreign or temporary resident` MEANS
    IF `discount testing period starts after 8 May 2012`
    THEN `discount percentage` ((`days I was an Australian resident and not a temporary resident` TIMES 100) DIVIDED BY (2 TIMES `days in the discount testing period`))
    ELSE IF `resident and not temporary on 8 May 2012`
         THEN `discount percentage` (((`days in the discount testing period` MINUS `days after 8 May 2012 I was a foreign or temporary resident`) TIMES 100) DIVIDED BY (2 TIMES `days in the discount testing period`))
         ELSE `not covered: the period starts on or before 8 May 2012 and you were then a foreign or temporary resident (s 115-115(4) to (6))`

-- itaa-cgt.l4's `What is my net capital gain` (s 102-5) on one discount capital gain at that percentage.
@export What is my net capital gain from one discount capital gain, as a foreign or temporary resident for part of the time (ss 102-5, 115-115)?
GIVEN `capital gain` IS A NUMBER @desc The discount capital gain, in dollars
      `losses applied` IS A NUMBER @desc Capital losses and earlier net capital losses applied to it, in dollars
      `discount testing period starts after 8 May 2012` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you acquired the asset after 8 May 2012
      `resident and not temporary on 8 May 2012` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were an Australian resident, and not a temporary resident, on 8 May 2012
      `days in the discount testing period` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days from acquisition to the CGT event
      `days I was an Australian resident and not a temporary resident` IS A NUMBER @desc The days in that period you were an Australian resident and not a temporary resident
      `days after 8 May 2012 I was a foreign or temporary resident` IS A NUMBER @desc The days in that period, after 8 May 2012, you were a foreign or temporary resident
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is my net capital gain as a part-time foreign or temporary resident` MEANS
    CONSIDER `What is my discount percentage as a part-time foreign or temporary resident` `discount testing period starts after 8 May 2012` `resident and not temporary on 8 May 2012` `days in the discount testing period` `days I was an Australian resident and not a temporary resident` `days after 8 May 2012 I was a foreign or temporary resident`
    WHEN `discount percentage` `p` THEN JUST (`What is my net capital gain` `capital gain` `losses applied` `p`)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING
